From 50113a0ea724d0bc633fbc37b743a205e1561caa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Garv <garvagnihotri22@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(onboarding): add the Loophole first-run onboarding

- new LoopholeOnboarding overlay (port of Void's VoidOnboarding.tsx as plain DOM, no React/Tailwind build step):
  1. welcome page with the animated logo and "Get Started"
  2. theme picker with Loophole Dark, Loophole Light, Dark 2026 and Light 2026; picking one applies it right away.
     The preview cards are drawn from the real theme colors.
  3. settings import from VS Code, Cursor and Windsurf (IExtensionTransferService), then "Enter Loophole"
- the provider page is dropped, the Kilo agent has its own sign-in and model setup.
- shown once on the first start (storage key loopholeOnboarding.completed), not with --skip-welcome.
  "Skip" is available until the last page. Re-open it with "Show Loophole Onboarding" (Help category, F1).
- if the imported settings.json does not set a theme, the theme picked on page 2 is applied again.
- follows the --vscode-* theme colors, honors reduced motion, keeps keyboard focus inside the overlay.
- the logo is a CSS mask of the Loophole mark (loophole-mark.svg), tinted with the foreground color.
